copyright and permission notice is retained verbatim in icu4c/ICU-LICENSE, and
the individual ICU source files retain their own per-file copyright headers.
The Unicode License V3 requires that this notice accompany all copies of the
ICU code and data; icu4c/ICU-LICENSE and those per-file headers satisfy that
requirement. No ICU file has been relicensed, and no ICU notice has been
removed.

Note: icu4c/ICU-LICENSE also reproduces third-party notices for various ICU
data components, some under BSD, MIT, or GPL-with-linking-exception terms.
Those notices cover ICU data categories -- for example the break-iterator
word dictionaries and transliteration data -- that are NOT included in the
collation-only data trim shipped in icu4c/icudt78l.dat (see icu4c/DATA.md).

